{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to express the base-10 integer \\( n \\) in terms of the bases \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). The number \\( 32_a \\) in base \\( a \\) can be converted to base-10 as:\n\\[ n = 3a + 2. \\]\nSimilarly, the number \\( 23_b \\) in base \\( b \\) can be converted to base-10 as:\n\\[ n = 2b + 3. \\]\nSince both expressions represent the same integer \\( n \\), we can set them equal to each other:\n\\[ 3a + 2 = 2b + 3. \\]\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\\[ 3a - 2b = 1. \\]\nWe need to find the smallest possible values of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) that satisfy this equation, with the conditions that \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are integers greater than 3. We can solve this equation using the method of finding particular solutions and then the general solution.\n\n","prefix_end":746,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,3158,279,2331,12,16,15,7546,17767,308,1124,8,304,3793,315,279,23092,17767,264,1124,8,323,17767,293,1124,568,576,1372,17767,220,18,17,4306,1124,8,304,2331,17767,264,1124,8,646,387,16099,311,2331,12,16,15,438,510,78045,308,284,220,18,64,488,220,17,13,1124,921,67691,11,279,1372,17767,220,17,18,880,1124,8,304,2331,17767,293,1124,8,646,387,16099,311,2331,12,16,15,438,510,78045,308,284,220,17,65,488,220,18,13,1124,921,12549,2176,23393,4009,279,1852,7546,17767,308,1124,701,582,646,738,1105,6144,311,1817,1008,510,78045,220,18,64,488,220,17,284,220,17,65,488,220,18,13,1124,921,49,682,81,8595,279,3793,11,582,633,510,78045,220,18,64,481,220,17,65,284,220,16,13,1124,921,1654,1184,311,1477,279,24632,3204,2750,315,17767,264,1124,8,323,17767,293,1124,8,429,26553,419,23606,11,448,279,4682,429,17767,264,1124,8,323,17767,293,1124,8,525,25780,7046,1091,220,18,13,1205,646,11625,419,23606,1667,279,1714,315,9271,3953,9904,323,1221,279,4586,6291,382,5338,11,582,1477,264,395